  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Namibia - National Society Development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Summary:
Namibia Chronic Hunger &amp; Organisational Development is a project to work with the Namibian Red cross to develop their food security strategy, social protection and disaster management to position them as the government&apos;s organisation of choice.This new partnership and will look at specific outcome of integrating the National Societies into the Governments Protection programmes and positions the NS as a partner of choice of its government.Working closely together and in close coordination with other RC partners and external stakeholders in Southern Africa to make a lasting difference to the lives of vulnerable communities suffering from Chronic Food insecurity.By capitalising on NRC&#x2019;s advantages in Namibia and effectively contributing to national social protection systems, NRC will be able offer systemic solutions to communities affected by disaster: and thereby to become the partners of choice for governments, donors and partner agencies in delivering assistance
Location: NamibiaBens: None at the moment &#x2013; mostly OD work&#xa0;&#xa0;Donor: None &#x2013; General funds&#xa0; PNSs: None
Budget:2019 Total - &#xa3;52K2020 Total - &#xa3;100K2021 Total - &#xa3;100K2022 Total -&#xa3;150K
Situation Update In 2019: funds were used to cover FSL role to work on FS plans and DM workshop.&#xa0;In 2020: Due diligence was completed in Feb 2020, from their an improvement plan has been create - however due to COVID these plans were put on hold&#xa0;In 2021: OD work will be planned off the back of the improvement plan - however these plans are currently on hold whilst we wait for FCDO to confirm funding for FBF.</narrative>
  </description>
